[0.9.0] 2026-09-21 — FIX — Reveal fail-safe (IntersectionObserver health probe)
================================================================================
Found during browser QA: every scroll-triggered reveal starts hidden and relies
on IntersectionObserver to bring it in. In the preview renderer IO callbacks
never fired, so headlines, plan cards and the fine-print grid stayed permanently
invisible. Any environment that starves IO — an embedded webview, an aggressive
prerenderer, a browser without IO — would have shipped a blank page.
- Added useIOHealth.ts: on first use it observes a throwaway 1px element. If no
  callback arrives within 900ms, IO is marked broken process-wide.
- Reveal, TextReveal, StaggerGrid, ClipWipe, PlanCard and FiberPath now take an
  `animate` override that drives them to their visible state when IO is broken.
  Healthy browsers are unaffected and keep the scroll-triggered behaviour.
- BlackHole no longer depends on IO alone to pause: the rAF loop rect-checks
  itself twice a second and stops when the hero scrolls away, with a passive
  scroll listener to resume. Previously, if IO never fired, the canvas would
  have animated forever behind the rest of the page.

