[2.1.0] 2026-09-21 — MEDIA — Photography added across the site
================================================================================
Seven images supplied, generated with Gemini (Nano Banana), delivered as PNGs at
1408x768 totalling 20.7 MB.

OPTIMISATION — 20.7 MB -> 0.71 MB (96.6% smaller), via sharp:
  hero-home           2620 KB -> 89 KB    fiber-install   2907 KB -> 119 KB
  bundle-living-room  2719 KB -> 75 KB    tv-fioptics     2825 KB -> 65 KB
  phone-kupuna        3285 KB -> 102 KB   why-neighborhood 3530 KB -> 157 KB
  og-share            3357 KB -> 120 KB (kept JPEG — some social scrapers still
                                         refuse WebP)
  Re-encoded at source resolution; no upscaling. PNG originals removed.

PLACEMENT
  Hero              full-bleed background, priority, blur placeholder
  Fiber             full-width band with an overlaid caption
  Bundles           split panel, image left
  TV                split panel, image right
  Phone             split panel, image left
  Why Hawaiian Telcom  full-width banner with an overlaid caption
  og-share          OpenGraph + Twitter summary_large_image metadata

IMPLEMENTATION
- Static imports throughout, so Next emits intrinsic dimensions and a blur
  placeholder at build time, and a missing or renamed file fails the build
  rather than shipping a broken image.
- ServiceSection gained an optional `media` prop (`band` | `split`, with a side)
  so all four service sections stay on one component.
- Every slot reserves its box before the image loads — no layout shift.
- Hero alt is intentionally empty: it is decorative and the headline beside it
  already carries the meaning. The six content images have descriptive alt.

FIXES FOUND WHILE WIRING
1. Hero photograph was invisible. The first scrim used Tailwind's evenly-spaced
   gradient stops, which kept the overlay near-opaque across the whole frame
   while the offer card covered the rest. Replaced with explicit colour stops
   (solid to 34%, gone by 66%) so the right half of the image reads.
2. Offer card had no background at all. `bg-white/92` is not a step Tailwind
   generates, so the class produced nothing and the card rendered transparent —
   small grey body copy over a busy photograph. Card is now solid white.
3. Band and banner captions were unreadable. Same root cause, worse effect:
   `from-ht-navy/92` failed to generate, which left --tw-gradient-from undefined,
   which invalidated the entire var(--tw-gradient-stops) chain and collapsed
   background-image to `none`. Both captions now use an explicit inline
   linear-gradient, which cannot fail this way.
4. Audited every opacity modifier in src/ and normalised the five remaining
   non-standard steps (/45 /55 /65 /85) to generated ones, removing the whole
   class of silent failure.
5. "neighbourhood" -> "neighborhood"; the site is US English throughout.

NOTED, NOT CHANGED
- Every image carries Gemini's visible sparkle watermark inset from the
  bottom-right, clearly visible on the hero. Left in place deliberately: it
  marks the image as AI-generated and removing it would strip a provenance
  signal. Regenerating on a tier that does not apply the visible mark is the
  correct fix. Invisible SynthID watermarking persists regardless.
- Source images are 1408px wide, so the hero is slightly soft on a 2x display.
  The white scrim hides this well.
- A laptop with a visible Apple mark appears in hero-home.webp. Incidental use,
  but this site publishes a Trademarks policy — worth a review before launch.

